[s0l0!-header][h1]Break[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

We've met the [b]break [/b]statement earlier in this module, we use it to "jump out" of a loop and continue executing the code after the loop.

[s0l0!-header][b]Like this:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="js" codeId="673"]for (i = 0; i <= 10; i++) {
   if (i == 5) {
     [b]break[/b]; 
   }
   document.write(i + "<br />");
}[/code]
In this example, once i reaches 5, it will break out of the loop. [img id="2758" width="100%"]
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
You can use the return keyword to return some value immediately from the loop inside of a function. This will also break the loop.
[/note]

