[s0l0!-header][h1]Continue[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

We're nearly done with module 3! One last thing to cover.

Unlike the [b]break[/b] statement, the [b]continue [/b]statement breaks only one iteration in the loop, and continues with the next iteration.

[s0l0!-header][b]Like this:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="js" codeId="674"]for (i = 0; i <= 10; i++) {
   if (i == 5) {
      [b]continue; [/b]
   }
   document.write(i + "<br />");
}[/code]
[s0l0!-header][b]Result: [/b][/s0l0!-header] [img id="2759" width="100%"]
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
The value 5 is not printed, because [b]continue [/b]skips that iteration of the loop.[/note]
